Package: lwdidR
Title: Lee-Wooldridge Difference-in-Differences via Unit-Specific Transformations
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Xiang", "Ao", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "xao@hbs.edu")
Author: Xiang Ao [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Xiang Ao <xao@hbs.edu>
Description: Implements the Lee and Wooldridge (2026) panel difference-in-differences
    estimator via unit-specific pre-treatment transformations (demean, detrend,
    demeanq, detrendq). Supports both common-timing and staggered adoption designs
    with cohort-specific aggregation. Inference options include homoskedastic OLS,
    HC1, HC3 (manual sandwich), cluster-robust, wild cluster bootstrap
    (Rademacher weights), and permutation/randomisation inference. The last two are
    distribution-free and recommended at small N or with non-normal errors.
    Replicates the staggered Castle Doctrine application (Section 7.2) of Lee and
    Wooldridge (2026b) (SSRN 5325686). This package is an R port of the original
    Stata 'lwdid' command by Lee and Wooldridge (<https://github.com/Soo-econ/lwdid>),
    whose v1.0 is based on that small-sample paper. The underlying outcome
    transformation is published in Lee and Wooldridge (2026)
    <doi:10.1080/07350015.2026.2683047>.
